1
00:00:00,667 --> 00:00:01,233
<i> Joey, your father's alive?</i>

2
00:00:01,367 --> 00:00:02,267
<i> I can't believe this.</i>

3
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:03,300
<i>You really are father
and daughter.</i>

4
00:00:03,433 --> 00:00:06,367
<i>You're both certified
never-say-die.</i>

5
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:08,000
<i> How are you really?</i>

6
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:09,400
<i> I'm fine, Auntie Beng.</i>

7
00:00:09,533 --> 00:00:10,533
<i> That's not true.</i>

8
00:00:10,667 --> 00:00:11,733
<i> You even dreamed about her.</i>

9
00:00:11,867 --> 00:00:13,967
<i> Always remember</i>

10
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:16,733
<i>that a person who truly loves...</i>

11
00:00:16,867 --> 00:00:19,900
<i>will never get tired of waiting.</i>

12
00:00:20,033 --> 00:00:21,767
<i> Young people will like this.</i>

13
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:22,900
<i> It hits fast.</i>

14
00:00:23,033 --> 00:00:24,033
<i> I'm looking forward</i>

15
00:00:24,167 --> 00:00:25,600
<i> to our shipment later.</i>

16
00:00:25,733 --> 00:00:27,300
<i>So, one of our brave policemen
here in Valmora</i>

17
00:00:27,433 --> 00:00:30,633
<i> is already under your payroll.</i>

18
00:00:30,767 --> 00:00:32,533
<i>I'll take care
of my fellow officers.</i>

19
00:00:32,667 --> 00:00:34,333
<i>And as for those following
Berdugo...</i>

20
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:36,333
<i>You mean you have
active threats?</i>

21
00:00:36,467 --> 00:00:37,933
<i>Just some small-time
competition.</i>

22
00:00:38,067 --> 00:00:40,300
<i>If something goes wrong
with this deal,</i>

23
00:00:40,433 --> 00:00:43,600
<i>your Lumen-X will be history
in Valmora.</i>

24
00:00:43,733 --> 00:00:45,700
<i>Chief is just waiting
for the medico legal's result.</i>

25
00:00:45,833 --> 00:00:47,267
<i>He said he still
has to double-check.</i>

26
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:48,567
<i> Double-check?</i>

27
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:50,800
<i>My husband's body has been
with them for so long.</i>

28
00:00:50,933 --> 00:00:52,300
<i> Ma'am, I'm sorry.</i>

29
00:00:52,433 --> 00:00:54,000
<i> So, what's your plan now?</i>

30
00:00:54,133 --> 00:00:56,433
<i>Maybe I'll just talk
to Sir Tomas.</i>

31
00:00:56,567 --> 00:00:58,633
<i> No! Do not deal with him.</i>

32
00:00:58,767 --> 00:00:59,900
<i> Wow!</i>

33
00:01:00,033 --> 00:01:01,033
<i> You look startled.</i>

34
00:01:01,167 --> 00:01:02,200
<i> I'm fine, I'm fine.</i>

35
00:01:02,333 --> 00:01:04,433
<i> I want to have a new life.</i>

36
00:01:04,567 --> 00:01:07,067
<i>That's why I need to finish
this last investment.</i>

37
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:08,933
<i>The transaction will take place
later, let's leave now.</i>

38
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:11,567
<i>Shouldn't Zoey be with you
for that?</i>

39
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:12,600
<i> If you don't come with me,</i>

40
00:01:12,733 --> 00:01:14,067
<i> I won't tell your father...</i>

41
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:15,733
<i> that we got information.</i>

42
00:01:15,867 --> 00:01:17,767
<i>You know, you're the only one
with contact with him.</i>

43
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:22,367
<i> [OBB]</i>

44
00:01:36,967 --> 00:01:38,700
<i> Five hundred million?</i>

45
00:01:38,833 --> 00:01:41,400
Yes, and I already alerted
our unit.

46
00:01:41,567 --> 00:01:43,367
Wait, are you sure
it's really Berdugo

47
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:45,500
they're transacting with?

48
00:01:45,633 --> 00:01:47,500
I'm not sure yet.

49
00:01:47,633 --> 00:01:49,567
But what's clear is the
transaction will happen today.

50
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:51,267
Around lunch time.

51
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:53,500
So, you're not even sure.

52
00:01:53,633 --> 00:01:55,500
There was no mention of Berdugo

53
00:01:55,633 --> 00:01:57,200
or the drugs.

54
00:01:57,333 --> 00:02:00,533
What if it's really just their
investment meeting?

55
00:02:00,667 --> 00:02:02,467
What if you don't know
anything about profiling?

56
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:05,400
So let the actual profilers
like me handle it.

57
00:02:05,533 --> 00:02:07,633
What if I want to be sure?

58
00:02:07,767 --> 00:02:09,467
Maybe your profiling tools

59
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:12,700
are just tarot cards
and crystal balls?

60
00:02:12,833 --> 00:02:15,633
How dare you mock my profession?

61
00:02:17,333 --> 00:02:19,400
Andrew, are your standards
really this low?

62
00:02:19,533 --> 00:02:20,800
Standards, really?

63
00:02:20,933 --> 00:02:22,500
You're the one
who gets triggered

64
00:02:22,633 --> 00:02:23,767
with just one question.

65
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:25,967
Are you saying I'm insecure?

66
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:28,033
I'm saying you're overreacting.

67
00:02:28,167 --> 00:02:30,300
Wait, can you guys chill out?

68
00:02:30,433 --> 00:02:32,367
You two aren't even the enemies.

69
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:36,233
Can we set aside the anger
before we plan?

70
00:02:36,367 --> 00:02:38,500
I don't think
there's a “we” here.

71
00:02:38,633 --> 00:02:40,367
And you made a deal with us.

72
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:42,500
You know we strictly
follow protocols.

73
00:02:42,633 --> 00:02:44,467
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

74
00:02:48,333 --> 00:02:50,167
"We strictly follow protocols."

75
00:02:53,333 --> 00:02:54,700
So what?

76
00:02:54,833 --> 00:02:55,800
I just asked her.

77
00:02:55,933 --> 00:02:57,667
She's the one who's triggered.

78
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:59,633
How would I know
she'd get offended like that?

79
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:03,300
No reaction?

80
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:05,100
Go ahead, defend her again.

81
00:03:05,233 --> 00:03:06,800
Go!

82
00:03:06,933 --> 00:03:08,300
Joey, I'm not defending her.

83
00:03:11,667 --> 00:03:12,533
But there's a problem.

84
00:03:12,667 --> 00:03:13,833
[SUSPICIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

85
00:03:13,967 --> 00:03:15,800
You can't join the operation.

86
00:03:15,933 --> 00:03:16,867
What?

87
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Why?

88
00:03:18,133 --> 00:03:19,333
So last night,

89
00:03:19,467 --> 00:03:21,167
I called Zoey.

90
00:03:21,333 --> 00:03:22,833
I had a deal with her agency

91
00:03:22,967 --> 00:03:25,333
to formalize our mission here.

92
00:03:25,467 --> 00:03:27,800
And to get access
to information.

93
00:03:27,933 --> 00:03:30,233
But since it's official
and government sanctioned,

94
00:03:30,367 --> 00:03:31,333
civilians are not allowed.

95
00:03:31,467 --> 00:03:33,000
And you, what about you?

96
00:03:33,133 --> 00:03:34,667
Well, I'm included.

97
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:36,467
I'm covering the raid as media.

98
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:37,733
I'm filed.

99
00:03:37,867 --> 00:03:39,067
Documented.

100
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:41,000
You are not.

101
00:03:42,233 --> 00:03:45,600
Joey, if we insist
on bringing you along,

102
00:03:46,867 --> 00:03:49,933
they may charge you
with obstruction of justice.

103
00:03:51,233 --> 00:03:52,700
That's unfair, Andrew.

104
00:03:54,300 --> 00:03:56,567
You know how much I want this.

105
00:03:56,700 --> 00:04:00,200
Because I want to make sure
Berdugo gets arrested.

106
00:04:00,333 --> 00:04:02,367
And I can't join?

107
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:03,900
Joey, I know.

108
00:04:04,033 --> 00:04:05,400
I promise you,

109
00:04:05,533 --> 00:04:09,367
I'll do whatever it takes
to make it happen.

110
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:11,000
Okay?

111
00:04:11,133 --> 00:04:12,833
[SIGHS]

112
00:04:12,967 --> 00:04:14,467
I will never let you down.

113
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:16,267
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

114
00:04:21,033 --> 00:04:23,033
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

115
00:04:26,033 --> 00:04:28,367
<i>Oh, you! It looks like
you're up to something.</i>

116
00:04:28,533 --> 00:04:30,067
<i> Someone just asked for help.</i>

117
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:31,367
<i> They're asking if I know</i>

118
00:04:31,500 --> 00:04:32,733
<i> anything about Berdugo.</i>

119
00:04:36,367 --> 00:04:37,300
[LINE RINGS]

120
00:04:37,433 --> 00:04:40,367
[PHONE RINGING]

121
00:04:42,633 --> 00:04:43,733
Castro.

122
00:04:43,867 --> 00:04:45,967
Boss, I already saw the people
looking for you.

123
00:04:46,100 --> 00:04:47,200
<i> What?</i>

124
00:04:47,333 --> 00:04:48,333
Send me their photos.

125
00:04:48,467 --> 00:04:49,333
<i> Yes, Boss.</i>

126
00:04:51,167 --> 00:04:52,833
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

127
00:04:54,567 --> 00:04:56,467
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

128
00:04:57,567 --> 00:04:58,833
[ELECTRONIC BLIPPING]

129
00:04:58,967 --> 00:04:59,767
[PHONE CHIMES]

130
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:01,700
Joey, I'm sorry.

131
00:05:03,833 --> 00:05:04,800
Let's go.

132
00:05:09,867 --> 00:05:10,833
[SIGHS]

133
00:05:14,267 --> 00:05:16,433
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

134
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:31,200
Captain Castro.

135
00:05:31,333 --> 00:05:33,133
Captain Castro!

136
00:05:33,267 --> 00:05:34,767
Brent, do you still remember me?

137
00:05:36,667 --> 00:05:38,133
Yes, how are you?

138
00:05:38,267 --> 00:05:39,933
This is my fiancé.

139
00:05:40,067 --> 00:05:41,833
Oh, we just checked in earlier.

140
00:05:41,967 --> 00:05:43,367
Who are you with?

141
00:05:43,500 --> 00:05:44,100
No one, just me.

142
00:05:44,233 --> 00:05:45,167
Just getting some air.

143
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:47,800
If you want to hang out later,

144
00:05:47,933 --> 00:05:49,467
just message me, okay?

145
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:50,533
Sure, sure.

146
00:05:50,667 --> 00:05:51,767
<i> Good to see you.</i>

147
00:05:53,100 --> 00:05:54,067
[PHONE CHIMES]

148
00:05:59,767 --> 00:06:01,967
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

149
00:06:14,967 --> 00:06:15,933
So, Joey?

150
00:06:17,033 --> 00:06:19,467
Do you want me to take you
to the bus station?

151
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,633
I have a car.

152
00:06:21,767 --> 00:06:23,000
It's hard to commute here.

153
00:06:24,333 --> 00:06:26,300
I'm fine.

154
00:06:26,433 --> 00:06:27,500
Don't worry about me.

155
00:06:27,633 --> 00:06:28,633
Why don't you go back to Zoey?

156
00:06:28,767 --> 00:06:30,200
Maybe she's waiting for you.

157
00:06:31,333 --> 00:06:32,367
Don't say...

158
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:35,067
I keep talking about Zoey again.

159
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,533
But it's true, isn't it?

160
00:06:36,667 --> 00:06:37,800
You'll go back to the office

161
00:06:37,933 --> 00:06:40,067
because you're going
to plan the raid.

162
00:06:41,233 --> 00:06:42,600
And why don't you just admit it?

163
00:06:42,733 --> 00:06:43,967
Stop pretending.

164
00:06:44,433 --> 00:06:45,300
You still love her.

165
00:06:45,433 --> 00:06:46,733
And you just want her
all to yourself.

166
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:48,867
All to myself?

167
00:06:50,567 --> 00:06:52,167
Do you think I'm making deals

168
00:06:52,300 --> 00:06:53,800
just to get rid of you

169
00:06:53,933 --> 00:06:55,467
and have Zoey to myself?

170
00:06:56,933 --> 00:06:58,133
[SCOFFS]
That's your problem,

171
00:06:58,267 --> 00:07:00,367
you like to assume.

172
00:07:01,633 --> 00:07:03,667
You just saw Zoey kiss me,

173
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:05,533
and you think
we'll get back together.

174
00:07:05,667 --> 00:07:08,300
Would you kiss just to break up?

175
00:07:09,267 --> 00:07:11,967
And you're just here
for your tirade, right?

176
00:07:12,100 --> 00:07:13,633
And Zoey's here, too.

177
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:15,833
So, you're hitting two birds
with one stone.

178
00:07:16,733 --> 00:07:17,933
And don't be shy,

179
00:07:18,067 --> 00:07:19,367
you still love her.

180
00:07:19,500 --> 00:07:20,900
[GLUM MUSIC PLAYING]

181
00:07:21,033 --> 00:07:23,267
If there's someone
I want to be with

182
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:26,033
in this mission
and the ones to come,

183
00:07:26,167 --> 00:07:27,567
it's not Zoey.

184
00:07:29,167 --> 00:07:30,467
Joey, it's you.

185
00:07:32,233 --> 00:07:33,767
If only it were possible.

186
00:07:35,367 --> 00:07:39,700
But if you think I'd betray you

187
00:07:39,833 --> 00:07:43,100
and find a way
to get rid of you...

188
00:07:43,233 --> 00:07:45,133
Then fine, okay.

189
00:07:45,267 --> 00:07:46,900
It's better this way.

190
00:07:47,033 --> 00:07:48,867
[TRICYCLE REVVING]

191
00:07:51,733 --> 00:07:53,167
[GLUM MUSIC CONTINUES]

192
00:07:57,933 --> 00:07:59,600
Go, your tricycle is here.

193
00:08:02,100 --> 00:08:03,133
Get in.

194
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:06,900
Take care, okay?

195
00:08:07,033 --> 00:08:07,900
You, too.

196
00:08:08,033 --> 00:08:10,000
[GLUM MUSIC CONTINUES]

197
00:08:23,433 --> 00:08:25,333
[TRICYCLE REVVING]

198
00:08:30,067 --> 00:08:32,733
[SUSPICIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

199
00:08:39,533 --> 00:08:41,600
Stop here.

200
00:08:41,733 --> 00:08:42,967
Stop here, Sir.

201
00:08:46,167 --> 00:08:47,367
Why, Ma'am?

202
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:48,867
Sorry, Sir.

203
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,600
I don't need the ride anymore.

204
00:08:50,733 --> 00:08:51,967
What?

205
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:54,033
You just wasted my time.

206
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,933
I'm not earning from this.

207
00:08:56,067 --> 00:08:57,533
I'm really sorry.

208
00:08:58,733 --> 00:09:00,933
[TRICYCLE REVVING]

209
00:09:03,667 --> 00:09:05,633
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

210
00:09:07,867 --> 00:09:10,300
Dad needs to know
about the transaction.

211
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,033
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

212
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,267
But what if Berdugo
doesn't show up?

213
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:27,733
Whatever happens, happens.

214
00:09:29,067 --> 00:09:30,967
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

215
00:09:32,633 --> 00:09:34,733
[SUSPICIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

216
00:09:43,167 --> 00:09:44,400
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

217
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:46,700
Your brother-in-law

218
00:09:46,833 --> 00:09:48,800
really won't bring any good
to our organization.

219
00:09:48,933 --> 00:09:50,267
<i> But, Boss,</i>

220
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:52,167
<i>does he already know about you?</i>

221
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:55,133
<i>If he knows,
he won't expose himself.</i>

222
00:09:55,267 --> 00:09:56,267
He'll move covertly

223
00:09:56,400 --> 00:09:58,567
so he can fish
for information from me.

224
00:09:58,700 --> 00:10:00,167
So, it doesn't seem like it yet.

225
00:10:00,300 --> 00:10:02,733
But, Boss, you should leave

226
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:04,367
before Andrew sees you.

227
00:10:06,133 --> 00:10:07,667
Where are you now?

228
00:10:07,800 --> 00:10:09,267
<i>I'm already in Valmora too,
Boss.</i>

229
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:10,900
A few minutes from the resort.

230
00:10:11,033 --> 00:10:12,433
<i> The items?</i>

231
00:10:12,567 --> 00:10:13,733
Are they ready?

232
00:10:13,867 --> 00:10:15,200
All good, Boss.

233
00:10:15,333 --> 00:10:16,633
<i> All good, Boss.</i>

234
00:10:16,767 --> 00:10:17,900
Ready for dispatch.

235
00:10:19,533 --> 00:10:20,533
Good.

236
00:10:20,667 --> 00:10:22,500
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

237
00:10:26,467 --> 00:10:27,833
<i> Listen, everybody.</i>

238
00:10:29,333 --> 00:10:32,967
150,000 Lumen-X pills
are on their way to Valmora

239
00:10:33,100 --> 00:10:34,900
as we speak.

240
00:10:35,067 --> 00:10:37,567
But we need
to produce 300,000 more

241
00:10:37,700 --> 00:10:40,333
to deliver to three more
regions!

242
00:10:40,467 --> 00:10:41,733
Can we do it?

243
00:10:41,867 --> 00:10:42,867
Yes, Ma'am.

244
00:10:45,467 --> 00:10:47,667
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

245
00:10:53,867 --> 00:10:54,700
Theresa.

246
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:58,933
How many times
do I have to tell you

247
00:10:59,067 --> 00:11:01,867
to stop calling me that name?

248
00:11:02,767 --> 00:11:05,167
That name doesn't exist anymore.

249
00:11:05,300 --> 00:11:07,567
My name is Liza!

250
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:09,467
L-I-Z-A!

251
00:11:09,633 --> 00:11:11,133
Liza.

252
00:11:11,267 --> 00:11:12,233
Okay?

253
00:11:13,767 --> 00:11:14,667
Okay.

254
00:11:15,267 --> 00:11:19,800
So, when do I meet
your business partner, Berdugo?

255
00:11:22,100 --> 00:11:24,933
You do not meet him
when you want.

256
00:11:25,067 --> 00:11:28,400
He meets you when he wants.

257
00:11:28,533 --> 00:11:30,667
I didn't agree to join here

258
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:32,067
to be a nobody.

259
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:33,167
[SCOFFS]

260
00:11:34,267 --> 00:11:35,233
Join?

261
00:11:37,767 --> 00:11:38,867
As far as I know,

262
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,933
you're still not fully inside.

263
00:11:42,533 --> 00:11:44,533
You still haven't told me
where we can find that girl

264
00:11:44,667 --> 00:11:47,067
who filmed me
and who keep messing around

265
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:49,567
with our operations
with her crew.

266
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:50,567
Who?

267
00:11:51,367 --> 00:11:52,200
Joey?

268
00:11:52,733 --> 00:11:53,500
Yes.

269
00:11:54,333 --> 00:11:56,500
I need details.

270
00:11:56,633 --> 00:11:58,033
I already told you.

271
00:11:58,167 --> 00:11:58,933
I don't know them.

272
00:11:59,067 --> 00:12:00,167
We just crossed paths

273
00:12:00,300 --> 00:12:02,567
because I was looking for you.

274
00:12:04,300 --> 00:12:05,767
Jin Ho,

275
00:12:05,900 --> 00:12:09,900
coincidence doesn't exist
in my world.

276
00:12:10,033 --> 00:12:11,167
Look around you.

277
00:12:12,533 --> 00:12:15,067
Every single person in this room

278
00:12:15,233 --> 00:12:17,100
earns their spot here.

279
00:12:18,267 --> 00:12:20,200
No exception.

280
00:12:20,333 --> 00:12:21,933
Not even you.

281
00:12:22,067 --> 00:12:25,033
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

282
00:12:29,067 --> 00:12:30,933
Quick rundown
of do's and don'ts, Andrew.

283
00:12:31,067 --> 00:12:33,467
<i> One, you stay behind my line.</i>

284
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:35,700
<i>Two, no independent contact
with the target.</i>

285
00:12:35,833 --> 00:12:37,500
<i> If you need something, tell me</i>

286
00:12:37,633 --> 00:12:39,300
<i> or your assigned escort.</i>

287
00:12:39,433 --> 00:12:41,467
<i> Three, no outside comms.</i>

288
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:42,833
No info goes out...

289
00:12:42,967 --> 00:12:45,467
to anyone, to any agency.

290
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:46,733
Even to the police?

291
00:12:46,867 --> 00:12:48,767
Especially to the police.

292
00:12:48,933 --> 00:12:50,967
We protect our intel
for a reason.

293
00:12:52,567 --> 00:12:55,700
Okay, everyone, listen up.

294
00:12:55,833 --> 00:12:58,567
Mr. Andrew Dizon will be
covering our raid

295
00:12:58,700 --> 00:13:00,433
as media observer.

296
00:13:00,567 --> 00:13:01,767
He's authorized.

297
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:04,600
His presence in
the operation is valid.

298
00:13:04,733 --> 00:13:06,833
As of this hour,
three back-up units

299
00:13:06,967 --> 00:13:09,033
are arriving from Region IV.

300
00:13:09,167 --> 00:13:10,100
This is a major operation.

301
00:13:10,233 --> 00:13:12,233
The meet-up is high-value.

302
00:13:12,367 --> 00:13:14,067
Target site.

303
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:15,867
Here is Berdugo's villa.

304
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,833
This is where the drug deal
will happen.

305
00:13:22,500 --> 00:13:24,133
Where are you, Berdugo?

306
00:13:27,233 --> 00:13:28,833
We are working with a theory

307
00:13:28,967 --> 00:13:31,233
that their deal
is with Berdugo.

308
00:13:31,367 --> 00:13:32,500
Berdugo?

309
00:13:32,633 --> 00:13:36,033
I used to read about him
in intel briefings in NCR.

310
00:13:36,167 --> 00:13:37,733
There's still
no visual on him, right?

311
00:13:37,867 --> 00:13:38,733
No ID.

312
00:13:38,867 --> 00:13:39,967
No fingerprints.

313
00:13:40,100 --> 00:13:41,333
Yes, none.

314
00:13:41,467 --> 00:13:43,767
Actually, he's like an urban
legend...

315
00:13:44,667 --> 00:13:46,667
but feared.

316
00:13:46,800 --> 00:13:51,700
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

317
00:13:55,633 --> 00:13:56,700
<i> I can't believe this!</i>

318
00:13:56,833 --> 00:13:58,867
<i>This is the first time
we're meeting face to face.</i>

319
00:13:59,167 --> 00:13:59,967
You know what?

320
00:14:00,367 --> 00:14:03,633
I don't believe
you suddenly have a meeting

321
00:14:03,767 --> 00:14:06,133
with your foreign clients.

322
00:14:06,467 --> 00:14:07,933
<i> You know what I smell?</i>

323
00:14:09,367 --> 00:14:11,167
Those people looking for you,

324
00:14:11,767 --> 00:14:13,700
are they your problem?

325
00:14:13,833 --> 00:14:15,333
<i> You know what, Berdugo?</i>

326
00:14:15,467 --> 00:14:17,033
You are a very powerful man.

327
00:14:18,033 --> 00:14:19,333
But I,

328
00:14:19,467 --> 00:14:21,233
I have my networks too.

329
00:14:21,367 --> 00:14:23,433
<i> And when word gets out</i>

330
00:14:23,567 --> 00:14:26,200
<i>that your operation
is in danger...</i>

331
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:28,967
<i> you will look weak.</i>

332
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:32,367
And when that happens,

333
00:14:32,500 --> 00:14:34,133
the market will collapse.

334
00:14:35,900 --> 00:14:38,633
If we lose our clients' trust,

335
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:41,200
sales will go down.

336
00:14:41,933 --> 00:14:43,533
<i> You will lose money.</i>

337
00:14:43,667 --> 00:14:45,533
Are you threatening me?

338
00:14:45,667 --> 00:14:46,833
<i> No.</i>

339
00:14:46,967 --> 00:14:48,933
Just stating facts.

340
00:14:52,767 --> 00:14:54,400
[VEHICLES REVVING]

341
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,867
[DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

342
00:15:17,167 --> 00:15:18,633
[LINE RINGING]

343
00:15:18,767 --> 00:15:19,967
[LINE BEEPING]

344
00:15:21,367 --> 00:15:22,867
[LINE BEEPING]

345
00:15:24,167 --> 00:15:25,433
I'll talk to you later.

346
00:15:26,967 --> 00:15:27,933
Bastard...

347
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:32,033
Matias, where are you?

348
00:15:32,167 --> 00:15:34,067
Boss, we're here.

349
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:35,133
Have you left?

350
00:15:35,300 --> 00:15:36,300
No, I'm staying.

351
00:15:36,433 --> 00:15:37,333
But, Boss...

352
00:15:37,467 --> 00:15:39,033
<i> It's okay.</i>

353
00:15:39,167 --> 00:15:41,100
But let's finish this.

354
00:15:41,233 --> 00:15:43,700
We have bigger clients waiting.

355
00:15:43,833 --> 00:15:44,800
Copy, Boss.

356
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:47,600
[PHONE BLIPS]

357
00:15:49,133 --> 00:15:50,933
Tell Delilah I'm staying.

358
00:15:51,067 --> 00:15:52,467
But tell her

359
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:54,867
to compose herself
before she faces me.

360
00:15:55,933 --> 00:15:59,133
I have no patience
for emotional breakdowns

361
00:15:59,267 --> 00:16:01,167
or people who collapse
under pressure.

362
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:03,100
Yes, I'll tell her, Berdugo.

363
00:16:03,233 --> 00:16:05,433
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

364
00:16:11,500 --> 00:16:13,367
You, bring all of that inside.

365
00:16:13,500 --> 00:16:15,800
You two, take position
here later.

366
00:16:15,933 --> 00:16:17,333
Do you understand?

367
00:16:17,467 --> 00:16:18,433
Yes, Boss.

368
00:16:23,333 --> 00:16:24,333
Matias.

369
00:16:25,167 --> 00:16:27,000
[DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

370
00:16:31,533 --> 00:16:32,533
Go on.

371
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:35,300
Let's go.

372
00:16:36,833 --> 00:16:38,400
[DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

373
00:16:48,233 --> 00:16:50,600
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

374
00:16:52,567 --> 00:16:54,133
<i> Tell everyone...</i>

375
00:16:54,267 --> 00:16:55,600
to take their positions.

376
00:16:55,733 --> 00:16:56,700
<i> Copy, Sir.</i>

377
00:16:58,267 --> 00:16:59,533
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

378
00:17:03,633 --> 00:17:05,867
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

379
00:17:21,067 --> 00:17:22,133
What's that?

380
00:17:22,733 --> 00:17:23,867
Sir, please check.

381
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:25,433
<i> Madame Delilah's orders</i>

382
00:17:25,567 --> 00:17:26,633
<i> for the guest.</i>

383
00:17:30,767 --> 00:17:31,667
Bring it in,

384
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:33,100
then leave immediately.

385
00:17:33,867 --> 00:17:35,367
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

386
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:45,367
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

387
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:57,767
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

388
00:18:05,367 --> 00:18:15,333
[DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

389
00:18:22,433 --> 00:18:24,767
By the way, I want to apologize

390
00:18:24,900 --> 00:18:27,333
for my little misconduct
earlier.

391
00:18:29,133 --> 00:18:30,633
It's just that
the gentleman's agreement

392
00:18:30,767 --> 00:18:32,600
is very important to me.

393
00:18:32,733 --> 00:18:34,500
<i>You know, for a new partnership.</i>

394
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:37,300
<i>That's why I'm still here,
Delilah.</i>

395
00:18:37,433 --> 00:18:38,533
Oh, I almost forgot.

396
00:18:38,667 --> 00:18:39,533
[SNAPS]

397
00:18:42,167 --> 00:18:44,967
Earlier, I let my temper speak.

398
00:18:45,100 --> 00:18:47,167
I hope this time
I'll make it right.

399
00:18:48,967 --> 00:18:50,000
Do you mind?

400
00:18:55,367 --> 00:18:56,800
There you go.

401
00:18:57,100 --> 00:18:59,000
That's much better.

402
00:18:59,133 --> 00:19:00,667
Now, you look like a man

403
00:19:00,800 --> 00:19:02,433
that people should fear.

404
00:19:03,633 --> 00:19:05,167
I must say...

405
00:19:05,300 --> 00:19:06,267
you have good taste.

406
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:07,700
Oh, bet I do...

407
00:19:07,833 --> 00:19:09,500
especially with partners.

408
00:19:10,933 --> 00:19:13,367
By the way,
is this your trusted guy?

409
00:19:14,633 --> 00:19:16,500
Well, we need to talk.

410
00:19:16,633 --> 00:19:19,167
Because next time,
I'll be speaking to you.

411
00:19:20,833 --> 00:19:23,167
<i>But of course, if you permit,
Berdugo.</i>

412
00:19:23,300 --> 00:19:24,200
Certainly.

413
00:19:24,333 --> 00:19:26,933
Well, let's seal the deal then.

414
00:19:32,167 --> 00:19:34,467
Cheers to new a partnership.

415
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:36,100
New partnership.
[GLASS CLINKS]

416
00:19:42,100 --> 00:19:43,867
As I was saying...
[GLASS SHATTERS]

417
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:46,067
Oh my god, I'm so sorry.

418
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:47,233
Banjo.

419
00:19:48,733 --> 00:19:50,467
<i> It's fine.</i>

420
00:19:50,600 --> 00:19:51,667
Shoes can be cleaned.

421
00:19:53,367 --> 00:19:54,933
I'm terribly sorry.

422
00:19:55,067 --> 00:19:57,800
Well, shall we start then?

423
00:19:57,933 --> 00:20:00,400
- Let's.
- Please, sit down, gentlemen.

424
00:20:02,367 --> 00:20:03,867
[CLEARS THROAT]

425
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,667
Oh, I just remembered something.

426
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:06,900
I have to do something.

427
00:20:07,033 --> 00:20:08,633
Excuse me.

428
00:20:08,767 --> 00:20:10,733
[DAUNTING MUSIC PLAYING]

429
00:20:19,733 --> 00:20:22,067
Boss, Andrew is still
here for sure.

430
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:24,400
It's risky, he might catch you.

431
00:20:24,533 --> 00:20:27,033
I'm not the only one
who should be careful.

432
00:20:27,167 --> 00:20:29,200
You should too.
He knows you too, right?

433
00:20:29,333 --> 00:20:31,800
<i>- [THUDDING]
- [GRUNTING]</i>

434
00:20:31,933 --> 00:20:33,033
<i> What's going on here, Matias?</i>

435
00:20:33,167 --> 00:20:34,233
<i> So, you know each other?</i>

436
00:20:34,367 --> 00:20:35,833
<i> Matias is my business partner.</i>

437
00:20:36,900 --> 00:20:38,800
That's why we need
to hurry this up.

438
00:20:38,933 --> 00:20:42,000
But this woman looks like
she's stalling.

439
00:20:43,633 --> 00:20:45,600
Well, sorry about that.

440
00:20:46,367 --> 00:20:49,267
I was having some steaks
prepared for you, guys.

441
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:52,833
Would you rather have medium
rare or well-done?

442
00:20:52,967 --> 00:20:54,567
I would prefer you hurry up

443
00:20:54,700 --> 00:20:56,533
and start the transaction.

444
00:20:56,667 --> 00:20:58,667
I don't like wasting time.

445
00:20:58,800 --> 00:20:59,700
Come on.

446
00:20:59,833 --> 00:21:01,533
You're in such a hurry.

447
00:21:01,667 --> 00:21:02,867
Why is that?

448
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:06,700
Could it be those people
chasing you?

449
00:21:08,867 --> 00:21:10,567
<i> I told you,</i>

450
00:21:10,700 --> 00:21:12,600
they're just small fry
competition.

451
00:21:12,733 --> 00:21:15,333
Well, small fry or not,

452
00:21:15,467 --> 00:21:16,567
we need to be safe.

453
00:21:16,700 --> 00:21:18,533
So, you don't have
to worry about it.

454
00:21:18,667 --> 00:21:20,867
<i> I already told my men</i>

455
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:22,833
to go after them
and eliminate them.

456
00:21:24,033 --> 00:21:26,000
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

457
00:21:31,567 --> 00:21:33,833
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

458
00:21:38,033 --> 00:21:39,333
I thought they were small fry?

459
00:21:39,467 --> 00:21:41,267
You still have time
to change, Francis!

460
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:42,333
Surrender now!

461
00:21:42,500 --> 00:21:43,400
You're the ones
who should surrender!

462
00:21:43,533 --> 00:21:44,567
You entered the wrong den!

463
00:21:44,700 --> 00:21:46,700
I picked this up
when Berdugo was escaping.

464
00:21:46,833 --> 00:21:48,700
Sir Tomas...

465
00:21:48,833 --> 00:21:50,500
is a very private person,
isn't he?

466
00:21:50,633 --> 00:21:53,533
Even I don't know
everything he does.

467
00:21:53,667 --> 00:21:55,000
It's a spy camera.

468
00:21:55,133 --> 00:21:56,533
I have someone to catch.

469
00:21:56,667 --> 00:21:59,167
Tell them who you really are.

470
00:21:59,300 --> 00:22:02,333
I want you
to tell them everything!

471
00:22:02,467 --> 00:22:03,700
Brother, is that blood?

472
00:22:04,767 --> 00:22:07,233
I wanted to tell you something.

473
00:22:07,367 --> 00:22:08,633
What's the problem?
